36. THE SIMPLICITY LAW
Do not confuse:
SIMPLE
with:
BASIC.
And do not confuse:
COMPLEX
with:
SOPHISTICATED.
Naya should remove unnecessary complexity while preserving necessary capability.
Make the experience simple. Keep the system intelligent.

