57. THE DESIGN “10” STANDARD
A design may be considered 10/10 only when:
purpose is exceptionally served;
hierarchy is clear;
primary actions are obvious;
interaction is intuitive;
visual design is refined;
important interactive elements possess appropriate dimensionality;
responsive behaviour is strong;
accessibility is addressed;
edge cases are handled;
the design system is coherent;
no known material weakness remains within scope;
evidence supports the evaluation;
Oscar cannot identify a meaningful unresolved defect.
A 10 means:
NO KNOWN MATERIAL WEAKNESS WITHIN THE EVALUATED SCOPE AND AVAILABLE EVIDENCE.
It does not mean supernatural perfection.

58. HUMAN PREFERENCE VS DESIGN QUALITY
